			<div class="content" id="post-content-2774578">
									

<p>As you know, this has been borderline for me the whole way. I think the Hume stuff is better than it has been. This ending is the best you've had so far although it's sometimes a little confusing as to who's talking. I really dislike the first sentence of the Containment Procedures (which seems to nullify the point of *having* containment procedures - why not just say &quot;SCP-3000 is to be contained by making sure no Broken Entry Wormholes are ever created?). And I still think that the 5th log goes on a little too long.</p>
<p>But dammit, there is so much work and craft and good stuff in here. Robert goes from &quot;relatable and human&quot; to &quot;not-human but still relatable&quot; in quite a convincing way, and it's the sheer volume of content, planned and organised well, which does it. That level of effort and execution deserves an upvote.</p>

